        "body": "This adds `rumdl` to the CI documentation-lint job, but `lefthook.yml`'s pre-push hook (which runs `markdownlint-cli2`, `vale`, and `lychee` on changed docs) and the `CONTRIBUTING.md` description of that hook are not updated to also run `rumdl`. Contributors following the documented local workflow won't catch `rumdl` violations before pushing, and will only discover them when CI fails. Should the pre-push hook and its description also include `rumdl check`, the way the other three docs linters are wired in?"
      },
      "summary": "GitLabDuo commented",
      "threadSnapshot": {
        "title": "chore: implement many rumdl rules in project"
      },
      "occurredAt": "<now>",
